body:
It might not actually be a deadlock. It might just be taking a really long time. If you comment out all of these sample_slots except one, the pipeline will compile within 5 seconds but for each sample_slot you uncomment, it takes an increasingly longer time. 

instances of the sample_slot function call not commented out     ->     time for pipeline compilation
1 -> within a second (might have been cached)
2 -> within a second (might have been cached)
3 -> ~40 seconds
4 -> ~ 1 minute and 45 seconds
5 -> ~ 2 minutes and 8 seconds
6 -> ~ 2 minutes and 42 seconds
7 -> ~ 4 minutes and 8 seconds
8 -> ~ 6 minutes and 20 seconds

There are 16 calls to that function in total in the led_lattice_v4_composite.gdshader shader, so the hang time increases quickly.

So based on my theory, I let the original MRP run to see if it would eventually compile, and it did after 26 minutes.

So with 16 calls of the sample_slots in the shader, it took 26 minutes and 33 seconds for the pipeline to finish compiling and stop hanging.

For example, eight of the calls are in this function:

```GDScript
vec3 composite_led_rgb(float cx, float cy, vec2 n) {
	vec4 best = vec4(0.0);
	float best_z = -100.0;
	bool hit = false;
	sample_slot(slot0_color, slot0_rect, slot0_stage, slot0_fx, slot0_meta, cx, cy, n, best, best_z, hit);
	sample_slot(slot1_color, slot1_rect, slot1_stage, slot1_fx, slot1_meta, cx, cy, n, best, best_z, hit);
	sample_slot(slot2_color, slot2_rect, slot2_stage, slot2_fx, slot2_meta, cx, cy, n, best, best_z, hit);
	sample_slot(slot3_color, slot3_rect, slot3_stage, slot3_fx, slot3_meta, cx, cy, n, best, best_z, hit);
	sample_slot(slot4_color, slot4_rect, slot4_stage, slot4_fx, slot4_meta, cx, cy, n, best, best_z, hit);
	sample_slot(slot5_color, slot5_rect, slot5_stage, slot5_fx, slot5_meta, cx, cy, n, best, best_z, hit);
	sample_slot(slot6_color, slot6_rect, slot6_stage, slot6_fx, slot6_meta, cx, cy, n, best, best_z, hit);
	sample_slot(slot7_color, slot7_rect, slot7_stage, slot7_fx, slot7_meta, cx, cy, n, best, best_z, hit);
	return hit ? best.rgb : vec3(0.0);
}
```

So this doesn't seem like an issue with Godot, and probably a performance issue in the Metal compiler. I will probably submit a bug report to Apple if this theory is reasonable to anyone else.

This is the troubling shader:

res://scripts/display/led_lattice_v4_composite.gdshader

If you change the led_lattice_v4_composite.gdshader at the end like this:

                                //halo = lattice_halo_composite(cx, cy, n, 0);
                                halo = vec3(0.0);

It starts up.
